    "final_answer": "Upgraded `payout_sync.py` from the v1 list endpoint to the v2 export API.\n\n**Changes**\n- Calls `GET /v2/payouts` instead of `/v1/payouts`.\n- Follows the opaque `cursor` until `drained` is true, rather than assuming one response contains everything.\n- Deduplicates on payout `id`, since v2 windows may overlap at their edges.\n- Handles a window returning fewer than `limit` payouts without ending early.\n- Restarts the export if the API rejects a cursor with `invalid_cursor`.\n- Uses `urllib.parse.urlencode`, so opaque cursors are encoded safely.\n\n**Verification against `http://the VM's public address:19121`**\n- Synced **2431 payouts**, all with unique ids.\n- Confirmed **0 duplicates** and all required payout fields present.\n- Independently compared the result to the live v1 snapshot: identical id sets **and** identical records.\n- Tested against a mock server covering overlapping windows, short/empty non-drained windows, and drain termination.",
